 "result_text": "I added `\"swimlane\"` to `UserStory.allowed_params` in `taiga/models/models.py`. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a Taiga server.\n\nThe cause was that `update()` only sends fields listed in `allowed_params`, and `swimlane` wasn't one of them. Every update therefore left the swimlane out of the request, and Taiga put the story back in Unclassified. With the field listed, `update()` sends the story's current swimlane back unchanged. It should also let you move a story by setting `story.swimlane` to a swimlane id, which didn't work before. I didn't test either behaviour.",
